WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.250
- So your husband does
something nice for you

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.240
with memorabilia,

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.260
like from the past.
- [Christina] Yeah.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.430
What is it? Can you explain?

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.770
- I have never saved
anything from my career,

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.930
anything, like, I don't
have my magazine covers

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:10.770
when I was younger.

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:13.290
I didn't save any of it.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.003
And he thinks that that's,

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.810
he like is encouraging me to be very proud

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.040
of my career and everything.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.680
So he's gone back and bought,
found them all on eBay

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:23.730
and bought them for me
(crowd aww)

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.128
and is like saving, I know, he's very,

00:00:26.128 --> 00:00:26.961
very sweet.
- It's kind of an

00:00:26.961 --> 00:00:27.870
amazing scrapbook too.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.000
I always think now as a
mom, like for your kids.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.833
- [Christina] Yeah.
- That's the only reason

00:00:30.833 --> 00:00:31.800
why I keep anything now, 'cause I'm like,

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.450
they might not care, but they might.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.770
I don't know.
- Yeah, it's true.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:35.603
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- When I was little

00:00:35.603 --> 00:00:37.740
I really cared about my mom's,

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:40.050
my mom was a model and so she had her book

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.130
with all her tear sheets,

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:42.540
and I really did care about that.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.680
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- So I get,

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.360
I get his point.
- Yeah.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.430
- About like the kids wanting it and

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:50.190
it also like it's nice,
and I think now that it's,

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.230
most of those magazine
covers are like 20 years old,

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.240
and now that I'm 20
years from that person.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.073
- It's like removed

00:00:55.073 --> 00:00:56.280
from it.
- I'm able to

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.930
be like, "Oh yeah, that was great."

00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:59.070
You know?
- Yeah.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:01.230
And you look, I always look
at things and people show me,

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:02.880
and I'm just like, oh my
God, I was like a baby.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.310
- Yeah, exactly, feels
like a different person.

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:06.600
- It really does.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:07.593
I love age.

